# Changelog

All notable changes to Two Leaves are documented here.

## [1.0.0] — First public release

### Core
- Chat UI for local Ollama models, built as a single self-contained HTML file.
- Full markdown rendering (code blocks, lists, links, bold/italic).
- Collapsible "Reasoning" section for models that output `<think>` blocks (e.g. Qwen3).
- Live connection status indicator and model picker, with a "Refresh models" button.

### Conversations
- Chats autosave locally in the browser and persist across sessions.
- Sidebar history list — reopen, right-click to export (copy as markdown) or delete (with confirmation).
- "New chat" button to start fresh.

### Speed
- Smart Speed Mode: optionally routes short messages (≤12 words) to a smaller/faster model automatically, falling back to a main model for longer prompts.
- Stop button to cancel a response mid-stream, keeping whatever had already generated.

### Design
- Custom cream/sage color theme with a background image and slow ambient pan/zoom.
- Material You–style motion: ripple feedback, spring-loaded toggle, animated modals and context menus.
- Collapsible "Advanced" settings panel to keep the everyday UI simple.
- Collapsible sidebar.

### Security
- Markdown output is sanitized with DOMPurify before rendering, closing an XSS gap where raw HTML in a model's response (or a misbehaving server) could otherwise execute.
- Error messages and server details are HTML-escaped before display.

---

Version numbers follow [Semantic Versioning](https://semver.org/): `MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH` — patch for fixes, minor for new features, major for breaking changes.
